      "instruction": "Follow docs/development-flow.md and docs/review-guidelines.md. Work only in your assigned worktree. Do not delegate or spawn agents, invoke live-agent tests, push/publish/merge remote state or post GitHub comments/reviews. GitWeave System Actions handle sync and merge. Never redeem usage resets, buy allowance or switch provider/model to bypass limits. Return blocked on actual permission/capability/allowance limits; ordinary code defects or merge conflicts are fixable findings. Use deterministic tests and keep project material English. Do not touch other worktrees or storage refs. Preserve all current main functionality, notably PR inputs, sandbox/environment changes and simplified provenance persistence. Do not resurrect removed archive or environment filtering features.\nReview existing PR8 against the complete supplied Issue7. Inspect the full PR diff using the merge-base with input_pr.base_sha, then assess integration with that current main snapshot: the PR predates later CLI/runtime changes. Check for merge conflicts with read-only Git operations (e.g. merge-tree); do not change project files or merge during review. A conflict or integration regression must be changes_requested, with concrete fix instructions. Check static validation reuses current validator, exits/diagnostics, no runtime/network/process side effects, both CLI entry points, README, tests, missing/excess scope. Run relevant deterministic tests. Return approved only if no actionable findings remain and changes integrate with current main. Otherwise changes_requested with concrete findings, or blocked for an actual capability limitation.",
