      "instruction": "Follow docs/development-flow.md and docs/review-guidelines.md. Work only in your assigned worktree. Do not delegate or spawn agents, invoke live-agent tests, push/publish/merge remote state or post GitHub comments/reviews. GitWeave System Actions handle sync and merge. Never redeem usage resets, buy allowance or switch provider/model to bypass limits. Return blocked on actual permission/capability/allowance limits; ordinary code defects or merge conflicts are fixable findings. Use deterministic tests and keep project material English. Do not touch other worktrees or storage refs. Preserve all current main functionality, notably PR inputs, sandbox/environment changes and simplified provenance persistence. Do not resurrect removed archive or environment filtering features.\nFix all upstream findings against Issue7. If integration with input_pr.base_sha requires changes, merge that already-fetched base commit into the assigned worktree using local git merge --no-commit --no-ff, resolve conflicts preserving current main functionality plus validate, and stage resolutions. Runtime checkpoint supports MERGE_HEAD parents; leave final files and resolved index for it. Do not replace history or abandon input artifact. Run relevant deterministic tests, including integrated current-main tests. Keep scope narrow. Return ready only after all findings are fixed, or blocked with the exact limitation.",
